  "narrative": "With direction -1, positive signed estimates indicate stronger CRISPR dependency in the exposed group. The approximate outcome_015 clinical threshold is about 0.0250. H86, feature_027=1 versus 0 within feature_010>=1 on outcome_015, is the only new result whose point estimate exceeds threshold: +0.0447, roughly 17.9% of the absolute outcome mean. However, its cell sizes are small and imbalanced (exposed 56, comparator 278), and the interval is very wide and crosses null: [-0.0111, 0.1004]. Because the discovery interval does not provide uncertainty support and this is one comparison among many, I do not accept it. I keep H86 unresolved and active but do not request validation: the small exposed cell and wide interval make independent validation likely inconclusive, and prior false-positive/validation failures warrant reserving validation for signals whose discovery interval itself points more clearly to clinically meaningful magnitude.\n\nH85, feature_010>=0, is weaker and less precise than the overall H76 result, with estimate +0.0156 [-0.0134, 0.0447], below threshold and crossing zero; reject and close. Cross-outcome coherence is poor: H87 outcome_005 gives opposite direction (-0.0172), H88 outcome_016 is near null (-0.0044), H89 outcome_007 is opposite (-0.0150), and H84 outcome_012 is null (+0.0033). H96 feature_027-by-feature_060 interaction is null (+0.0144 [-0.0242, 0.0531]). Taken together, these make H76 feature_027=1 versus 0 on outcome_015 unlikely to be a robust clinically meaningful main effect, so I reassess H76 as rejected and closed based on its own borderline estimate plus these non-coherent follow-up contrasts.\n\nThe other screens are not clinically meaningful. H90 feature_034 outcome_005 is positive but only +0.0102 and crosses zero; H91 feature_034 outcome_016 is opposite; H92/H93 feature_054 are null; H94 feature_055 outcome_005 is null/opposite. I reject and close these exact comparisons. The next step is targeted testing of the sole H86 context signal: whether feature_027 has a genuine feature_010>=1 interaction versus its complement, and whether the same context replicates on outcome_005, outcome_016, and outcome_007. If those remain inconsistent or imprecise, H86 should be closed. All conclusions remain observational associations in the supplied dataset.",
  "research_notes": "No accepted claims. H86 remains the only unresolved candidate: feature_027=1 vs 0 on outcome_015 within feature_010>=1, signed +0.0447 [-0.0111,0.1004], point above outcome_015 threshold ~0.0250 but exposed cell only 56 and interval crosses zero. No validation requested because validation would likely be too imprecise. H76 main-effect feature_027/outcome_015 is now rejected/closed because H85 broad context, coherence outcomes H84/H87/H88/H89, and H96 feature_060 interaction did not support a robust clinically meaningful main effect. Reject/closed this wave also includes H85,H87,H88,H89,H84,H96,H90-H94. Next follow-up: registered proposals test feature_027 interaction by feature_010>=1 on outcome_015 and coherence of feature_027 within feature_010>=1 on outcome_005/outcome_016/outcome_007. If no consistent positive interval-centered context effect, close H86. Avoid validation until a discovery interval itself is centered near or above clinically meaningful magnitude. Continue stable-outcome broad screens, but deprioritize noisy outcome_014/outcome_006 main-effect screens unless a strong lead emerges.",
